  <UserdefinedSymbols/>
  <Comments>LIJ1 Speedrun Practice Cheat Table by Sonic7
Made with Cheat Engine 7.2
---------------------------------------------------
Hooking into LIJ1:
 - Choose the Select process button 
   in the top left (computer icon)
 - Select LIJ1 executable
 - Confirm the LUA script if asked
---------------------------------------------------
Enable NOCUT:
Activating this box will enable NOCUT. Disabling the
box will turn off NOCUT.
----------------------------------------------------
Giving players items:
To select which item to give, double click the value column
for the player's selected item row. For player 1, double
click the "P1 Selected Item" value dropdown and choose the
item you want. To give the item, check the Give player item
box. For player one, check "Give P1 item".
----------------------------------------------------
Default Hotkeys:
Lift Player 1: B
Lift Player 2: N
Player 1 under floor: X
Player 2 under floor: CTRL+X
Teleport P1 to P2: Y
Teleport P2 to P1: U
Teleport P1 to Hard Spawn: I
---------------------------------------------------
Notes on player order:
"Player 1" refers to the player that started a hard load as player 1.
"Player 2" refers to the player that started a hard load as player 2.
"Player 3" refers to a character that started not dropped in but still is playable. (Example: Brody in 3-1 R1)
"Player 4" refers to a character that started not dropped in but is still is playable. (Example: Henry in 3-6 R1)
--------------------------------------------------
Notes on Extras section:
These seem to be similar structure to players but correspond to enemies and similar. Not sure if it is useful or relevant but it looks cool.
--------------------------------------------------
To rebind hotkeys:
- Lift Player 1:
     - Right click on "P1 Y Velocity"
     - Click "Set/Change Hotkeys"
     - Double click the hotkey
     - Type the hotkey you want into the box
     - Optional, if you want different lift:
           - Change the value under "Set value to"
- Lift Player 2:
     - Right click on "P2 Y Velocity"
     - Click "Set/Change Hotkeys"
     - Double click the hotkey
     - Type the hotkey you want into the box
     - Optional, if you want different lift:
           - Change the value under "Set value to"
- Player 1 under floor:
     - Right click on "P1 Y Position"
     - Click "Set/Change Hotkeys"
     - Double click the hotkey
     - Type the hotkey you want into the box
     - Optional, if you want to go lower:
           - Change the value under "Set value to"
- Player 2 under floor:
     - Right click on "P2 Y Position"
     - Click "Set/Change Hotkeys"
     - Double click the hotkey
     - Type the hotkey you want into the box
     - Optional, if you want to go lower:
           - Change the value under "Set value to"
 - Teleport P1 to P2:
     - Click "Table" at the top bar
     - Click "Show Cheat Table LUA Script"
     - Scroll up to the top
     - Set "P1_TO_P2_HOTKEY" equal to key you want
     - Note: CE uses Windows Virtual Key codes
 - Teleport P2 to P1:
     - Click "Table" at the top bar
     - Click "Show Cheat Table LUA Script"
     - Scroll up to the top
     - Set "P2_TO_P1_HOTKEY" equal to key you want
     - Note: CE uses Windows Virtual Key codes
- Teleport P1 to P1 Hard Spawn:
     - Click "Table" at the top bar
     - Click "Show Cheat Table LUA Script"
     - Scroll up to the top
     - Set "P1_TO_HARDSPAWN_HOTKEY" equal to key you want
     - Note: CE uses Windows Virtual Key codes
Setting a give item hotkey:
 - Right click the give item box of the player you want.
 - select Set hotkeys
 - Click create hotkey
 - choose the key
 - Set the dropdown to "Enable script"
 - Click apply 
----------------------------------------------------
Cheat Table notes:
Freezing values:
Check the box next to a memory value to freeze it.
Weapon instances ammo:
When picking up weapons, the game cycles between a
few memory addresses to store your weapon's current
ammo. Pick up a weapon, figure out which memory 
address isn't 0 and freeze it or change its value.
Hard Spawn watching:
If a player sets a new hard spawn, that players' 
Hard Spawn group label will light up pink in the
cheat table. This is useful for knowing if and 
where you set a hard spawn while setting up 
superjumps. To change how long the label lights 
up for, go into the LUA Script and change 
"TIMER_FLASH_AMOUNT" (default 1 second)
Superjump timer:
This value counts up to 2ish if the player is stuck.
When it reaches 2ish the player will superjump.
----------------------------------------------------
Setting up speedhack (Slow down the game):
 - Select “Edit” at the top
 - Select “Settings”
 - Select Hotkeys
 - Choose “Toggle the speedhack” and set hotkey
 - Go back to the main CE page
 - Check the “Enable Speedhack” box on the right
 - Set the value to what you want (Like 0.25)
 - Now you can toggle the speedhack with hotkey
----------------------------------------------------
Enable respawn speedup:
This enables auto-speedup when player 1 dies. Enable
this if you get impatient when dying. This will
overwrite your previous speedhack value if enabled.
----------------------------------------------------
</Comments>
  <LuaScript>TIMER_FLASH_AMOUNT = 1000 -- how long hard spawn flashes pink.



P1_TO_P2_HOTKEY = VK_Y -- Hotkey to teleport p1 to p2. default is VK_Y (Y)
P2_TO_P1_HOTKEY = VK_U -- Hotkey to teleport p2 to p1. default is VK_U (U)

P1_TO_HARDSPAWN_HOTKEY = VK_I -- Hotkey to teleport p1 to their hard spawn.
                              -- default is VK_I (I)

P1_WRITE_TO_TARGET_HOTKEY = VK_J -- Hotkey to write to target tp. default N

P1_TO_TARGET_HOTKEY = VK_H -- Hotkey to tp to target tp. default H

local addressList1 = getAddressList()


 -- Allocate give item memory
ai1 = getAddressList().getMemoryRecordByDescription("AllocItemP1")
ai2 = getAddressList().getMemoryRecordByDescription("AllocItemP2")
ai3 = getAddressList().getMemoryRecordByDescription("AllocItemP3")
ai4 = getAddressList().getMemoryRecordByDescription("AllocItemP4")

ai1.Active=true
ai2.Active=true
ai3.Active=true
ai4.Active=true



local function findHeaderByDescription(desc)
    for i=0, addressList1.Count-1 do
        local entry = addressList1[i]
        if entry.Description == desc then
            return entry
        end
    end
    return nil
end



-- values for nocut swapping
local headerNameNOCUTEnable = "Enable NOCUT"
local headerNameNOCUTDisable = "Disable NOCUT"
local memoryAddressNOCUT = "006A025C"

local valueWhenActiveNOCUT = 0x01F08313
local valueWhenNotActiveNOCUT = 0x1FF8C113


local headerNOCUTEnable = findHeaderByDescription(headerNameNOCUTEnable)
local headerNOCUTDisable = findHeaderByDescription(headerNameNOCUTDisable)

-- local P1ItemsBoxes = findHeaderByDescription("Give P1 items")

local p1itembox = findHeaderByDescription("Give P1 item")
local p2itembox = findHeaderByDescription("Give P2 item")
local p3itembox = findHeaderByDescription("Give P3 item")
local p4itembox = findHeaderByDescription("Give P4 item")

local function updateItemMemAlloc()
      ai1.Active=true
      ai2.Active=true
      ai3.Active=true
      ai4.Active=true
      end


if not (headerNOCUTEnable and headerNOCUTDisable) and false then
   print("NOCUT Header not found")
else
    -- update NOCUT memory here
    local function updateValueNOCUT()
          if headerNOCUTEnable.Active then
             writeInteger(memoryAddressNOCUT, valueWhenActiveNOCUT)
          else
              writeInteger(memoryAddressNOCUT, valueWhenNotActiveNOCUT)
          end

    end
local timerNOCUT = createTimer(nil, true)
local timerMem = createTimer(nil, true)
timerMem.Interval = 1000
timerNOCUT.Interval = 500
timerNOCUT.OnTimer = updateValueNOCUT
timerMem.OnTimer = updateItemMemAlloc
end


local headerSkipCutscene = findHeaderByDescription("Skip cutscene (bind hotkey)")
local endCutsceneTrack = findHeaderByDescription("End cutscene track")


-- update NOCUT memory here
    local function skipCutscene()
          if not headerSkipCutscene.Active then
             writeInteger(memoryAddressNOCUT, valueWhenActiveNOCUT)
             sleep(20)
             writeInteger(memoryAddressNOCUT, valueWhenNotActiveNOCUT)
             headerSkipCutscene.Active = false
          end
    endCutsceneTrack.Active = true
    endCutsceneTrack.Active = false
end

headerSkipCutscene.OnActivate = skipCutscene

local function updateItemsBoxes(item)
      if item then
         item.Active = false
      end
end

-- Script to disable the boxes of give items
local function disableItemBoxes()

      p1itembox.Active = false

      p2itembox.Active = false

      p3itembox.Active = false

      p4itembox.Active = false
end


local timerItems = createTimer(nil, true)
timerItems.Interval = 250
timerItems.OnTimer = disableItemBoxes

local GROUP_NAME = "P1 Hard Spawn"
local WATCHED = { "P1 X Hard Spawn", "P1 Y Hard Spawn", "P1 Z Hard Spawn" }

local hardSpawnSoundBox = getAddressList().getMemoryRecordByDescription("Hard Spawn sound")


local al = getAddressList()
local group = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(GROUP_NAME)

if not group then
  error("Group not found: " .. GROUP_NAME)
end

-- Store original color
local originalColor = group.Color
local lastValues = {}

-- Initialize last known values
for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED) do
  local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
  if rec then
    lastValues[name] = rec.Value
  end
end

local flashTimer = nil

local function flashGroup()
  -- group.Color = 0xFFC0CB -- pink
  group.Color = 0xFE019A -- bright pink

  if flashTimer then
    flashTimer.destroy()
  end

  flashTimer = createTimer()
  -- how long we are pink
  flashTimer.Interval = TIMER_FLASH_AMOUNT
  flashTimer.OnTimer = function(t)
    group.Color = originalColor
    t.destroy()
    flashTimer = nil
  end
end

-- Watch timer
local watchTimer = createTimer()
watchTimer.Interval = 50
watchTimer.OnTimer = function()
  for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED) do
    local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
    if rec then
      local current = rec.Value
      if lastValues[name] ~= current then
        lastValues[name] = current
        flashGroup()
        break
      end
    end
  end
end

-- P2 script for hard spawn watching
local GROUP_NAME_P2 = "P2 Hard Spawn"
local WATCHED_P2 = { "P2 X Hard Spawn", "P2 Y Hard Spawn", "P2 Z Hard Spawn" }

local al = getAddressList()
local groupP2 = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(GROUP_NAME_P2)

if not groupP2 then
  error("Group not found: " .. GROUP_NAME_P2)
end

-- Store original color
local originalColorP2 = groupP2.Color
local lastValuesP2 = {}

-- Initialize last known values
for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED_P2) do
  local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
  if rec then
    lastValuesP2[name] = rec.Value
  end
end

local flashTimerP2 = nil

local function flashGroupP2()
  groupP2.Color = 0xFE019A -- bright pink

  if flashTimerP2 then
    flashTimerP2.destroy()
  end

  flashTimerP2 = createTimer()
  -- how long we are pink
  flashTimerP2.Interval = TIMER_FLASH_AMOUNT
  flashTimerP2.OnTimer = function(t)
    groupP2.Color = originalColorP2
    t.destroy()
    flashTimerP2 = nil
  end
end

-- Watch timer
local watchTimerP2 = createTimer()
watchTimerP2.Interval = 50
watchTimerP2.OnTimer = function()
  for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED_P2) do
    local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
    if rec then
      local current = rec.Value
      if lastValuesP2[name] ~= current then
        lastValuesP2[name] = current
        flashGroupP2()
        break
      end
    end
  end
end

-- P3 script
local GROUP_NAME_P3 = "P3 Hard Spawn"
local WATCHED_P3 = { "P3 X Hard Spawn", "P3 Y Hard Spawn", "P3 Z Hard Spawn" }

local al = getAddressList()
local groupP3 = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(GROUP_NAME_P3)

if not groupP3 then
  error("Group not found: " .. GROUP_NAME_P3)
end

-- Store original color
local originalColorP3 = groupP3.Color
local lastValuesP3 = {}

-- Initialize last known values
for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED_P3) do
  local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
  if rec then
    lastValuesP3[name] = rec.Value
  end
end

local flashTimerP3 = nil

local function flashGroupP3()
  groupP3.Color = 0xFE019A -- bright pink

  if flashTimerP3 then
    flashTimerP3.destroy()
  end

  flashTimerP3 = createTimer()
  -- how long we are pink
  flashTimerP3.Interval = TIMER_FLASH_AMOUNT
  flashTimerP3.OnTimer = function(t)
    groupP3.Color = originalColorP3
    t.destroy()
    flashTimerP3 = nil
  end
end

-- Watch timer
local watchTimerP3 = createTimer()
watchTimerP3.Interval = 50
watchTimerP3.OnTimer = function()
  for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED_P3) do
    local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
    if rec then
      local current = rec.Value
      if lastValuesP3[name] ~= current then
        lastValuesP3[name] = current
        flashGroupP3()
        break
      end
    end
  end
end


-- P4 script
local GROUP_NAME_P4 = "P4 Hard Spawn"
local WATCHED_P4 = { "P4 X Hard Spawn", "P4 Y Hard Spawn", "P4 Z Hard Spawn" }

local al = getAddressList()
local groupP4 = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(GROUP_NAME_P4)

if not groupP4 then
  error("Group not found: " .. GROUP_NAME_P4)
end

-- Store original color
local originalColorP4 = groupP4.Color
local lastValuesP4 = {}

-- Initialize last known values
for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED_P4) do
  local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
  if rec then
    lastValuesP4[name] = rec.Value
  end
end

local flashTimerP4 = nil

local function flashGroupP4()
  groupP4.Color = 0xFE019A -- bright pink

  if flashTimerP4 then
    flashTimerP4.destroy()
  end

  flashTimerP4 = createTimer()
  -- how long we are pink
  flashTimerP4.Interval = TIMER_FLASH_AMOUNT
  flashTimerP4.OnTimer = function(t)
    groupP4.Color = originalColorP4
    t.destroy()
    flashTimerP4 = nil
  end
end

-- Watch timer
local watchTimerP4 = createTimer()
watchTimerP4.Interval = 50
watchTimerP4.OnTimer = function()
  for _, name in ipairs(WATCHED_P4) do
    local rec = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription(name)
    if rec then
      local current = rec.Value
      if lastValuesP4[name] ~= current then
        lastValuesP4[name] = current
        flashGroupP4()
        break
      end
    end
  end
end

-- hotkey for teleport p1 to p2 and p2 to p1:

local al = getAddressList()

local p1 = {
  x = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P1 X Position"),
  y = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P1 Y Position"),
  z = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P1 Z Position")
}

local p2 = {
  x = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P2 X Position"),
  y = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P2 Y Position"),
  z = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P2 Z Position")
}

local p1_hardspawn = {
  x = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P1 X Hard Spawn"),
  y = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P1 Y Hard Spawn"),
  z = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("P1 Z Hard Spawn")
}

-- Safety check
for k, v in pairs(p1) do
  if not v then error("Missing P1 " .. k) end
end
for k, v in pairs(p2) do
  if not v then error("Missing P2 " .. k) end
end
for k, v in pairs(p1_hardspawn) do
  if not v then error("Missing P1 HS " .. k) end
end

-- Teleport functions
local function teleportP1toP2()
  if p1.x.Value ~= nil then
    p1.x.Value = p2.x.Value
    p1.y.Value = p2.y.Value
    p1.z.Value = p2.z.Value
  end
end

local function teleportP2toP1()
  if p2.x.Value ~= nil then
    p2.x.Value = p1.x.Value
    p2.y.Value = p1.y.Value
    p2.z.Value = p1.z.Value
  end
end

local function teleportP1toHardSpawn()
  if p1.x.Value ~= nil then
    p1.x.Value = p1_hardspawn.x.Value
    p1.y.Value = p1_hardspawn.y.Value
    p1.z.Value = p1_hardspawn.z.Value
  end
end

-- Checking to make sure the hotkeys are not null
if P1_TO_P2_HOTKEY ~= nil then
   HK_P1_TO_P2 = createHotkey(teleportP1toP2, P1_TO_P2_HOTKEY)
end

if P2_TO_P1_HOTKEY ~= nil then
   HK_P2_TO_P1 = createHotkey(teleportP2toP1, P2_TO_P1_HOTKEY)
end

if P1_TO_HARDSPAWN_HOTKEY ~= nil then
   HK_P1_TO_HS = createHotkey(teleportP1toHardSpawn, P1_TO_HARDSPAWN_HOTKEY)
end

local triggered = false

-- === CONFIG ===
local SPEED_VALUE = 20
local SPEED_DURATION = 500 -- milliseconds
local CHECK_INTERVAL = 10 -- ms

-- Use ONE of these:

-- Option A: memory record
local healthMR = getAddressList().getMemoryRecordByDescription("P1 Health")

-- Option B: raw address (comment Option A if using this)
-- local healthAddress = 0x12345678

-- =================

local headerForRespawnSpeedup = getAddressList().getMemoryRecordByDescription("Enable respawn speedup")

local checkTimer = createTimer(nil, false)
checkTimer.Interval = CHECK_INTERVAL

checkTimer.OnTimer = function()
    local health

    if healthMR then
        health = tonumber(healthMR.Value)
    else
        health = readInteger(healthAddress)
    end

    if headerForRespawnSpeedup.Active then
      if health == 0 and not triggered then
          triggered = true

          -- Enable speedhack
          speedhack_setSpeed(SPEED_VALUE)

          -- Disable speedhack after 0.25s
          local offTimer = createTimer(nil, false)
          offTimer.Interval = SPEED_DURATION
          offTimer.OnTimer = function()
              speedhack_setSpeed(1)
              offTimer.destroy()
          end
          offTimer.setEnabled(true)
      end

      -- Reset trigger if health goes above 0 again
      if health &gt; 0 then
          triggered = false
      end
      end
end
checkTimer.setEnabled(true)


-- Motorcycle escape motorcycle fix

local fixMotorcyclesHeader = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("Fix endroom motorcycles")

if fixMotorcyclesHeader then
   fixMotorcyclesHeader.OnActivate = function(memoryrecord, before, currentstate)
     if not before then
        memoryrecord.Value = "1"
     end

     return true
  end
end



local muteCutscenesHeader = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("Mute cutscene (_NOSOUND)")

if muteCutscenesHeader then
   -- Create a single function to handle both on and off states
   local function toggleMute(memoryrecord, before, currentstate)
      if not before then
         if currentstate then
            memoryrecord.Value = "1" -- Box was checked -&gt; Mute on
         else
            memoryrecord.Value = "0" -- Box was unchecked -&gt; Mute off
         end
      end
      return true
   end

   -- Assign the function to both the activation and deactivation events
   muteCutscenesHeader.OnActivate = toggleMute
   muteCutscenesHeader.OnDeactivate = toggleMute
end

local fadeoutCutscenesHeader = al.getMemoryRecordByDescription("Fadeout audio on cutscene skip")

if fadeoutCutscenesHeader then
   -- Create a single function to handle both on and off states
   local function toggleFadeout(memoryrecord, before, currentstate)
      if not before then
         if currentstate then
            memoryrecord.Value = "1" -- Box was checked -&gt; Mute on
         else
            memoryrecord.Value = "0" -- Box was unchecked -&gt; Mute off
         end
      end
      return true
   end

   -- Assign the function to both the activation and deactivation events
   fadeoutCutscenesHeader.OnActivate = toggleFadeout
   fadeoutCutscenesHeader.OnDeactivate = toggleFadeout
end



</LuaScript>
